, \"t476\", \"t477\"], \"why\": \"The finding identifies the discontinued-stock half of P6: the buyer ignores discontinued dates and keeps buying retired equipment, which is then marked down. Purchase orders for the 2015 cohort ran at 5,505 units in 2025, and the 2023 cohort fell to 2,604 in 2023 before rising again to 9,956 in 2025 (t476). In 2025 those two cohorts carried $1,281,005 + $3,454,074 of stock-line markdown at a margin of -$767,211 - $2,022,425 = -$2,789,636, which matches the finding's -$2,789,637 (t477). It does not cover the other half of P6: spring stock-outs from forecasting without a seasonal index, and short lines filled by transfer (the key gives 186,712 short lines, 122,649 filled by transfer). The truth schema has no P6 table (t475), so these figures come from the warehouse.\"}"}},"tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011W6vvr1VoJTfUKsedWLM9A","display_name":"Save","server_display_name":"analyst","tool_name":"save"}]}
